-- `l4 batch` prints the checked module back, annotations included, and checks
-- it again. This wording runs over two lines with the second at the margin;
-- printed with its line break, the continuation lands at the margin again and
-- ends the definition, so every row failed. The printer puts it on one line.

@export default f
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the f` [the f of
%n%] n MEANS n PLUS 1
